Package: mcglmgraph
Type: Package
Title: Graphical Multivariate Covariance Generalized Linear Models
Version: 0.8.6
Authors@R: c(
    person(c("Jose", "Evandeilton"), "Lopes", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "evandeilton@gmail.com"),
    person(c("Wagner", "Hugo"), "Bonat", role = c("aut", "cph"),
           email = "wbonat@ufpr.br",
           comment = "Author of the MCGLM framework that this package extends"))
Description: Graph-structured modeling of the covariance between responses in
    Multivariate Covariance Generalized Linear Models (MCGLM), for Gaussian
    and non-Gaussian responses. The method, MCGLM-Graph, is fitted in two
    stages. The first stage fits the marginal MCGLM and extracts its Pearson
    residuals. The second stage imposes a graph on the covariance of these
    residuals and estimates the graph parameters with the Pearson estimating
    functions of the MCGLM, without a joint likelihood. Three layers are
    available: Gaussian graphical models (GGM), whose precision matrix is a
    linear predictor and whose zeros are null partial correlations; directed
    acyclic graphs (DAG), based on the modified Cholesky decomposition of
    Pourahmadi (1999) <doi:10.1093/biomet/86.3.677> under a fixed ordering of
    the responses; and completed partially directed acyclic graphs (CPDAG),
    learned by partial-correlation tests or by greedy equivalence search. A
    missing edge is read as absence of second-order conditional association,
    which coincides with conditional independence under joint normality of
    the residuals. Tools include structure selection by stepwise search, L1
    penalization and information criteria adjusted by the effective
    dimension, Wald tests, a variance that propagates the first-stage
    uncertainty as in Murphy and Topel (1985)
    <doi:10.1080/07350015.1985.10509471>, stability and bootstrap resampling,
    and structure recovery metrics. Analytical derivatives are implemented in
    C++ via 'RcppArmadillo'. The MCGLM framework is described in Bonat and
    Jorgensen (2016) <doi:10.1111/rssc.12145> and Bonat (2018)
    <doi:10.18637/jss.v084.i04>.
URL: https://github.com/evandeilton/mcglmgraph,
    https://evandeilton.github.io/mcglmgraph/
BugReports: https://github.com/evandeilton/mcglmgraph/issues
